      "writtenOn": "2023-03-28T15:24:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why is Skia involved here at all?\n\nCopying into a WebGPU texture from a StaticBitmapImage that is not created with WebGPU-compatible shared image flags.\n\nChrome makes an intermediate SharedImage that is shareable with both Skia and Dawn.\n\nThen, we use Skia to do source -\u003e intermediate, and Dawn to do intermediate - destination.",
      "parentUuid": "b92929c8_2cddf50f",
      "revId": "0c4eceec9bdf68ae94bd90319373f7e8372ddb0b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
